think The mechanism: pond/apps/lantern_face.rye imports lantern/lantern_core.rye (the pond-side room resolves the local copy) and gains two functions. face_kind_for maps a lantern Response to a FaceKind under the seam's ruling -- err_stop or an empty completion answers unknown, everything else answers proposed -- and face_from_response composes the face from a question and a Response, discarding an error stop's fragment (a fragment is not an answer) and passing width refusals through by name. The ruling is Lantern's own contract made structural: a machine's finished answer arrives as PROPOSED, and settled is earned by a witness, never by the sampler -- proven over the whole StoppedReason enum by a loop asserting face_kind_for never returns settled, and on metal by feeding the real pinned fixture lantern/fixtures/completion.bron through parse_fixture into the face: the row reads back ". use init.garden not ArgIterator" under "= proposed". Twelve legs GREEN; the witness gains two asserts; TAME clean.
